      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's generally not recommended to combine sertraline with over-the-counter (OTC) medications like cough syrup containing dextromethorphan without consulting your doctor. Dextromethorphan can interact with sertraline and potentially increase the risk of serotonin syndrome, a potentially life-threatening condition. To be safe, consider discussing your cough issues with your doctor or pharmacist, and they can advise you on the best course of action. They may also recommend alternative cough medications or treatments.",
